# A static fixture page the tests/Browser suite writes in beforeEach and deletes in
# afterEach. Ignored because that afterEach does NOT run when the process dies
# first — a band killed at its bound, a crash, a Ctrl-C — and an untracked
# leftover is fatal to the NEXT run: local-ci's worktree-drift gate (UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#1889)
# refuses to validate any worktree whose paths differ from the commit under test,
# so one interrupted run blocks every branch queued behind it. That was
# survivable while the browser suite was opt-in; UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#1727 puts it in the default
# gate, where it runs every time and, being LAST in the chain, is the one an
# interrupt is most likely to land on.
#
# An ignore rule is the right shape HERE and only here: `public/` holds build
# output, and the `__*_fixture.html` prefix is reserved. It was NOT the right shape
# for the suite's blueprint, collection and user writes, which landed in tracked
# source trees where a glob can mask a genuine file — UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#1920 relocated those into
# storage/framework/testing instead (Tests\Support\BrowserWriteIsolation), so
# nothing is written to hide.
/public/__*_fixture.html
/public/storage
/public/vendor/app
/public/vendor/seo-pro
/public/vendor/statamic
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
# Stored form submissions: what people typed into a form, never committed (UAMS-Web/uams-statamic-archive#2817)
/storage/forms
/storage/phpstan
/vendor
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.phpunit.result.cache
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
.DS_Store
/auth.json
/.fleet
/.idea
/.nova
/.zed

